Subject: [PATCH 28/34] [3.1.1] [M156] Prevent out-of-bounds marker reads
 during highlight painting

Original change's description:
> Prevent out-of-bounds marker reads during highlight painting
>
> Undo/redo and deleting text can leave an empty find-in-page marker. When
> uppercasing expands a character into several letters that wrap across
> lines, painting can read past the marker list while checking that empty
> boundary. Nothing matches at that boundary, so returning no matches
> prevents the invalid read while keeping the text and markers intact;
> that piece still appears, but without a search highlight.
>
> The tests recreate the editing and line wrapping that caused the crash
> and check that valid search matches are still returned at different
> points in the text. They also confirm that the text can be drawn without
> crashing, but do not check the exact appearance of the highlight.
>
